# What `vercel` uploads from the REPOSITORY ROOT.
#
# https://midnightpassport.com is deployed by `vercel --prod` run here, at the
# root. The Vercel project's Root Directory is `examples/passport-demo` and
# "Include source files outside of the Root Directory" is on, so the builder
# gets this whole tree and the build can reach `examples/passport-balancer`,
# `demo-backend`, `packages/connect`, and the root lockfile — none of which
# live under the app.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE THE CLI FALLS BACK TO .gitignore. That fallback is not
# something to rely on when the upload is the build's only input, so the rules
# are written out here. It is a DENY list: anything not named is uploaded, so a
# new workspace is included by default rather than silently missing.
#
# Nothing outside the workspaces above is a build input any more. The
# account-custody prototype that used to sit at the root, and the
# `isomorphic-ws` shim the demo once aliased into it, were retired on
# 2026/09/15; the shim now lives in the app, at `src/lib/ws-shim.ts`.

node_modules
.git
.vercel
dist
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# EVERYTHING BELOW IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and it has to be. This
# file takes .gitignore syntax, where a bare name matches at EVERY level: a
# rule reading `src` would withhold `examples/passport-demo/src`,
# `demo-backend/src`, and `packages/connect/src` — the whole build — rather
# than the one directory at the root it was meant to name. The rules above are
# bare on purpose; those names are generated or tooling output wherever they
# appear.

# Prose. Nothing under here is read by a build.
/docs

/src
/contracts
/run-all.sh

# THE GENERATED ZK TREES, EXCLUDED ON PURPOSE — this is the load-bearing part.
#
# A working copy that has built the demo carries ~250 MB of prover keys, ZKIR,
# and SRS slices under these paths. Uploading them would make what ships depend
# on what happens to be on the laptop, which is the whole failure this deploy
# path exists to end. The builder fetches them instead, from a pinned release
# asset (`scripts/zk-artefacts.lock.json`) and from the upstream bucket, and
# verifies the first against the tracked contract manifests. So the upload is
# the same whether or not anyone has ever built here.
examples/passport-balancer/contracts-stagenet/managed/*/keys
examples/passport-balancer/contracts-stagenet/managed/*/zkir
examples/passport-demo/public/zk
examples/passport-demo/public/zk-params
examples/passport-demo/contracts/stagenet
examples/passport-demo/.generated

# Local state and credentials, in case a working copy carries them.
.env
.env.local
.planning
.serena
